  "docTitle": "Task / Job Scheduler (Delayed, Periodic, DAG) - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Design a task scheduler: one-off, delayed and periodic jobs, priorities, retries with backoff, DAG dependencies, cancellation and a worker pool with a dispatcher that waits on conditions, in Java, Python and C++14.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">Read 65 min</span><span class=\"chip\">Build 120 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine-coding case study</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Rank 26 of 45</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Task / Job Scheduler (Delayed, Periodic, DAG)</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">The \"real concurrency\" case study. We start with an alarm clock and a kitchen, end with an in-memory scheduler that runs delayed, periodic and dependent jobs on a bounded worker pool, with priorities, retries and cancellation, and we prove it with 8 threads submitting 8,000 jobs at once. Java, Python and a C++14 simulation, all compiled and run.</p>\n"
  },
